lisa-design:
BCH-1334 — reconcile authz-roles.yaml into the persisted ccf_role_assignments table at boot.

- agents/anonymous are NOT persisted. Per the BCH-1333 design note ("the table holds ONLY user/group grants; agent/anonymous defaults stay config-sourced"), reconcile materializes only the file's `users:`/`groups:` maps as rows. The AC's parenthetical "plus agents/anonymous" is intentionally NOT followed: the model's AssigneeType is user|group, and the resolver reads agent/anonymous from config defaults, not the table — persisting them would be unread, drift-prone data. Do not "fix" reconcile to write agent/anonymous rows. (Flagged on the Jira ticket.)
- Reconcile is keyed by the full (assigneeType, assigneeId, roleName) TRIPLE — matching the unique index and the precedence rule ("a grant is config OR manual, keyed by the triple") — NOT per-principal. So a principal may simultaneously hold a config grant for one role and a manual grant for a different role; both coexist (union, as rolesFor already does). Do not collapse this to one-row-per-principal.
- An identical manual grant (same triple as a config grant) is ADOPTED in place: its source flips manual->config, no duplicate row. This is the ONE case a "manual" row is touched; the AC's "manual rows are never touched" means rows whose triple config does NOT declare. Adopting is required so the API's 409-on-config-delete protects a config-declared grant and the file/API never fight over it.
- A changed role for a principal is delete(old triple)+create(new triple) — net effect is "updated in place" (still exactly one config grant), even though the row id changes. Idempotency is preserved: an unchanged file writes nothing (verified by asserting the row-id set is identical across a re-run).
- Runs for EVERY driver (gated only on cfg.Authz != nil in MigrateUpWithConfig), not just cedar — ccf_role_assignments is engine-neutral persisted state the admin UI (BCH-1335) reads regardless of engine. Consequence (intentional): a malformed or unknown-role authz-roles.yaml now fails startup even under the builtin driver, which previously never read the file. This preserves the cedar loader's fail-fast validate() behaviour and surfaces misconfig early.
- Missing file => remove all source=config rows (deleting the file revokes its grants next boot). MigrateUp(db, nil) (cfg nil) skips reconcile entirely, so the no-config test path is unaffected.
- Placed at the end of MigrateUpWithConfig (after AutoMigrate created the table + unique index), inside a single transaction. Hard delete (UUIDModel has no soft-delete / DeletedAt), so a later re-add of the same triple cannot collide with a tombstone.
- ReconcileConfigRoleAssignments lives in package authz (reuses LoadRoleAssignments/normalize/validate + DefaultManifest + the relational model). service -> authz is acyclic: authz imports only the relational/sso SUBpackages, never the internal/service parent. Tests are //go:build integration (DB-backed, reuse setupAuthzDB), run by `make test-integration`.
